  "id": "Compound::DB01181 - Gene::1551",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Ifosfamide may influence Cyp3a7, a key enzyme in drug metabolism. The core pathway involves Ifosfamide binding to Cyp3a4 or Cyp2c18, both of which participate in Aromatase Activity, which is then recognized by Cyp3a7. This indicates that Ifosfamide may modulate the activity of Cyp3a7 through the regulation of Aromatase Activity, potentially altering the metabolic clearance of substrates. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The overlapping involvement of multiple cytochrome P450 enzymes in Aromatase Activity implies that Ifosfamide could exert its effects through a shared metabolic pathway, possibly by inhibiting or modulating the activity of these enzymes. This mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple binding sites and the hierarchical participation of enzymes in the same metabolic process.",
